"in either $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/system/bin/scripts OR $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps"
"/<app-name>/bin/scripts. \\\n"
"The search id is used to create a path to the search's results. All other"
" args are passed to the \\\n"
"script (unvalidated) as follows: \\i\\\\\n"
"$0 = scriptname \\i\\\\\n"
"$1 = number of events returned \\i\\\\\n"
"$2 = search terms \\i\\\\\n"
"$3 = fully qualified query string \\i\\\\\n"
"$4 = name of saved splunk \\i\\\\\n"
"$5 = trigger reason (i.e. \"The number of events was greater than 1\") "
"\\i\\\\\n"
"$6 = link to saved search \\i\\\\\n"
"$7 = DEPRECATED - empty string argument \\i\\\\\n"
"$8 = file where the results for this search are stored(contains raw "
"results)"
msgstr ""
"Comando interno usato per eseguire allarmi basati su script. Il file script deve risiedere \\\n"
"in $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/system/bin/scripts OPPURE in $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/<app-name>/bin/scripts. \\\n"
"L'ID di ricerca serve per creare un percorso verso i risultati della ricerca. Tutti gli altri argomenti vengono passati \\\n"
"allo script (senza verifica) come segue: \\i\\\\\n"
"$0 = scriptname \\i\\\\\n"
"$1 = numero di eventi restituito \\i\\\\\n"
"$2 = termini della ricerca \\i\\\\\n"
"$3 = stringa completa della query \\i\\\\\n"
"$4 = nome dello splunk salvato \\i\\\\\n"
"$5 = motivo dell'attivazione (ad es. \"The number of events was greater than 1\") \\i\\\\\n"
"$6 = link alla ricerca salvata \\i\\\\\n"
"$7 = OBSOLETO - argomento con stringa vuota \\i\\\\\n"
"$8 = file in cui sono memorizzati i risultati di questa ricerca (risultati non elaborati)"

